<title>JAPAN: Japan May gold imports down 19.4 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan May gold imports down 19.4 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in May fell by 19.4 percent from a year earlier to 9.59 tonnes, Ministry of Finance (MOF) data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			   May 97     Apr 97  May 96</p>
<p> Total		   9.59	 8.64    11.89</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> South Africa	  3.60	 1.05     1.58</p>
<p> South Korea	   2.30	 0.50     0.40</p>
<p> Australia	     2.05	 1.08     3.91</p>
<p> Switzerland	   1.09	 0.92     0.91</p>
<p>Cumulative gold imports in the first five months of 1997 totalled 59.59 tonnes, down from 66.14 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431</p>
</text>
